      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's perfect, it really sharpens the thesis. I want to push this even further in the next section. \n\nI'm thinking of arguing that the movement isn't just \"wrong\" in its logic, but that it's actually fundamentally incompatible with any form of modern, progressive civilization. I want to frame the nationalist faction as a relic of a primitive era that's fundamentally incapable of participating in a modern democracy. How can I weave that into the essay to make the argument feel inevitable and logically sound?",
